=== 5. the only exact bridge: residue-level-gap lemma ===
  f1^2 >= M0(Lam - Rbar)/(Lam - m1^2),  Rbar = M1/M0,  Lam = inf supp(nu - f1^2 delta)
  two-level case: equality (tautology) -> the lemma returns w1 itself, no new info
  rho^2= 2.28: w1_lb = (rho^2 - rbar)/(rho^2 - 1),  rbar = Rbar/m1^2
       rbar= 1.10 -> w1 >= 0.9219  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 1.50 -> w1 >= 0.6094  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 1.90 -> w1 >= 0.2969  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 2.28 -> w1 >= 0.0000  <-- vacuous
  rho^2= 2.48: w1_lb = (rho^2 - rbar)/(rho^2 - 1),  rbar = Rbar/m1^2
       rbar= 1.10 -> w1 >= 0.9324  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 1.50 -> w1 >= 0.6622  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 1.90 -> w1 >= 0.3919  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 2.48 -> w1 >= 0.0000  <-- vacuous
  rho^2= 2.68: w1_lb = (rho^2 - rbar)/(rho^2 - 1),  rbar = Rbar/m1^2
       rbar= 1.10 -> w1 >= 0.9405  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 1.50 -> w1 >= 0.7024  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 1.90 -> w1 >= 0.4643  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 2.68 -> w1 >= 0.0000  <-- vacuous
  rho^2= 5.79: w1_lb = (rho^2 - rbar)/(rho^2 - 1),  rbar = Rbar/m1^2
       rbar= 1.10 -> w1 >= 0.9791  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 1.50 -> w1 >= 0.8956  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 1.90 -> w1 >= 0.8121  >= r0 OK
       rbar= 5.79 -> w1 >= 0.0000  <-- vacuous
  => a floor on w1 from rho^2 needs Rbar = M1/M0, which is NOT measured anywhere;
     with rbar -> rho^2 the bound degrades to 0.  So (c)-part: measure M1/M0 (time-moment).

